---
/**
 * The intro paragraph of a course review page (spec S05 "The review page"):
 * what the page asks, the answer formats the course's items use, and what
 * Hint and Give up do. A component of its own so the Container API test can
 * render it without StarlightPage (issue #517). The format names are the
 * checkpoint kind ids of spec S01 "Interaction types", which has no other
 * learner-facing names. The script joins them with ", " and builds the
 * sentence, so no space depends on source whitespace, which the compiler
 * drops at a tag's line edge.
 */
import { CHECKPOINT_KIND_LABEL, labelOf } from '@lib/labels-fr';
import { checkpointsOf, getLessons } from '@lib/lessons';

interface Props {
	area: string;
}

const { area } = Astro.props;
const lessons = await getLessons(area);
// Every kind the page may ask: the reviewable `first` checkpoints and their `review` alternates.
const formats = [
	...new Set(
		lessons.flatMap((l) =>
			checkpointsOf(l, { alternates: true })
				.filter((c) => c.phase !== 'practice' && c.reviewable)
				.map((c) => c.kind),
		),
	),
];
const formatText = formats.length
	? `Ce parcours les pose sous ces formes : ${formats.map((f) => labelOf(CHECKPOINT_KIND_LABEL, f)).join(', ')}.`
	: 'Ce parcours n’a pas encore de question à poser.';
---

<p data-review-intro>
	Les questions des leçons terminées reviennent à des intervalles croissants. {formatText} <strong>Indice</strong> donne un coup de pouce. <strong>Voir la réponse</strong> montre la réponse après un essai, et la question compte comme échouée.
</p>
